00:21:00.760 --> 00:21:01.500
I'm very fond of her.

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:03.690
You like her, don't you?

00:21:04.170 --> 00:21:05.320
She's charming.

00:21:06.110 --> 00:21:06.830
That makes it mutual.

00:21:07.270 --> 00:21:08.090
She thinks you're very lovely.

00:21:09.930 --> 00:21:13.350
You know, I'd like you and her and all of us to see a lot of each other when we get back to London.

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:15.240
Oh, how nice.

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:24.940
My Paris officer's snowed me under with letters and telegrams.

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:25.520
Will you excuse me?

00:21:25.640 --> 00:21:28.320
I have a long morning's work ahead of me.

00:22:46.380 --> 00:22:51.020
Oh, Mr. Rushworth, you must have finished your work sooner than you expected.

00:22:51.530 --> 00:22:52.750
No, rather, I haven't finished any other.

00:22:53.420 --> 00:22:54.160
I said you like it.

00:22:55.750 --> 00:22:56.010
Lovely.

00:22:58.500 --> 00:22:59.420
Mr. Rushworth, you mustn't.

00:23:25.250 --> 00:23:29.080
There's a catch attached to the catch.

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:29.880
I mean the grasp.

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:32.060
Press the bottom of the cameo and it springs open.

00:23:32.360 --> 00:23:32.520
See?

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:32.920
Ooh.

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:35.790
Wicked-looking female, isn't she?

00:23:36.170 --> 00:23:37.050
Why, they're rubies.

00:23:37.600 --> 00:23:41.280
The lady inside said that the class once belonged to Marie Antoinette.

00:23:41.650 --> 00:23:42.130
Oh, wonderful.

00:23:42.570 --> 00:23:44.330
I told her I hope it'd bring you better luck than they brought her.

00:23:44.780 --> 00:23:45.200
Thank you.

00:23:45.380 --> 00:23:47.420
I'll never dare say that I like anything again.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:01.160
Telegrams for you, Rouen, sir?

00:24:01.580 --> 00:24:04.920
This one's for you, too, from Rouen.

00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:05.960
Oh, there's nothing wrong.

00:24:08.070 --> 00:24:09.450
Tremendous affair here tomorrow.

00:24:10.070 --> 00:24:12.010
French president unveiling monument.

00:24:12.520 --> 00:24:14.400
So I suggest you both motor here tonight

00:24:14.400 --> 00:24:17.790
and join us at Grandet Hill, Charlotte Channel.

00:24:19.250 --> 00:24:20.190
With the pile of work I've got,

00:24:20.230 --> 00:24:21.170
I couldn't leave till the morning,

00:24:21.230 --> 00:24:22.090
but if you'd like to...

00:24:22.500 --> 00:24:25.120
Well, I hate to face that three-hour drive alone

00:24:25.120 --> 00:24:27.180
and with the storm coming up, I...

00:24:27.200 --> 00:24:28.420
Yes, the morning's probably best.

00:24:30.060 --> 00:24:31.300
We'll have a quiet little dinner together.

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:32.810
That would be nice.

00:24:33.480 --> 00:24:35.030
Shall we say, uh, a pop-up date?

00:24:45.480 --> 00:24:46.100
Good evening, madam.

00:24:54.050 --> 00:24:54.330
Evening.

00:24:55.720 --> 00:24:56.120
Good evening.

00:25:02.810 --> 00:25:05.920
How lovely. So this is your secret tank?

00:25:06.270 --> 00:25:10.860
This is it. And you're the only guest who's ever come through that door.

00:25:10.980 --> 00:25:12.180
Not even your cousin Charlotte.

00:25:12.660 --> 00:25:16.410
Charlotte, peace to all. Once she got the honour of this cabin, I'd never get her out.

00:25:19.450 --> 00:25:20.130
No, Miss Crayon.

00:25:22.330 --> 00:25:22.970
Not even Bella.

00:25:24.070 --> 00:25:25.110
I feel awfully privileged.

00:25:30.160 --> 00:25:42.580
A bit.

00:25:56.990 --> 00:25:58.860
Look, I like the old lamp.

00:26:00.570 --> 00:26:01.210
I'll do it, Paul.

00:26:31.500 --> 00:26:35.320
I've always believed that the most despicable thing a man can do is to make love to another man's wife.

00:26:37.590 --> 00:26:38.290
Better be ashamed.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:02.570
just as soon as he can manage a long weekend.

00:27:02.750 --> 00:27:05.030
The poor darling's awfully busy with his new job

00:27:05.030 --> 00:27:07.250
and very grateful to you for getting it for him.

00:27:07.470 --> 00:27:09.530
So he's dying to come down and tell you so himself.

00:27:10.110 --> 00:27:11.230
That's really charming.

00:27:11.490 --> 00:27:12.190
Goodbye, Ivy.

00:27:12.720 --> 00:27:14.300
Goodbye, Lady Flora, and thank you again.

00:27:27.450 --> 00:27:28.710
Not my lucky day, Emily.

00:27:29.230 --> 00:27:29.970
Unlucky it comes.

00:27:30.280 --> 00:27:31.640
Lucky in love, they say, ma'am.

00:27:33.670 --> 00:27:35.070
Mr. Jarvis is nice, isn't he?

00:27:35.210 --> 00:27:36.010
That he is.

00:27:36.150 --> 00:27:36.790
The nicest.

00:27:37.780 --> 00:27:39.460
I thought you handled the party very well.

00:27:39.890 --> 00:27:41.210
It's a pleasure, I'm sure, ma'am.

00:27:41.510 --> 00:27:43.910
I said to Mr. Jenks, that's our lift man.

00:27:44.130 --> 00:27:45.910
I said we're really seeing life

00:27:45.910 --> 00:27:49.770
since Mr. Rushworth let Mr. and Mrs. Lex and his aunts flat.

00:27:50.010 --> 00:27:51.890
Oh, it will be dull when they come back.

00:27:52.140 --> 00:27:53.580
They gave parties, didn't they?

00:27:53.860 --> 00:27:56.160
Then, little tea parties, surely.

00:27:56.500 --> 00:27:58.680
Oh, well, yes, in a manner of speaking,

00:27:59.060 --> 00:27:59.980
when Mr. Rushworth would...

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:02.350
come down here with Miss Bella. Miss Bella?

00:28:02.550 --> 00:28:05.420
Well, poor Africa, that was. Did

00:28:05.420 --> 00:28:07.760
Mr. Rushworth come here often with Miss Bella?

00:28:07.980 --> 00:28:10.020
Of course. Why, of course?

00:28:10.700 --> 00:28:12.940
Well, see, she was Mr. Rushworth's young lady.

00:28:13.560 --> 00:28:14.580
They're not engaged.

00:28:16.120 --> 00:28:18.040
But everyone can see which way the wind's

00:28:18.040 --> 00:28:20.620
blowing. Do you really think that

00:28:20.740 --> 00:28:22.460
Mr. Rushworth will marry Miss Bella?

00:28:23.290 --> 00:28:25.910
That's my belief when he comes back from Africa.

00:28:30.280 --> 00:28:32.910
I'll answer it.

00:28:32.970 --> 00:28:33.550
Thank you, ma'am.

00:28:33.690 --> 00:28:37.230
Then I'll just pop over for a moment to see how my sister's face ache is.

00:28:37.390 --> 00:28:38.230
It'll be spanned.

00:28:38.450 --> 00:28:39.090
Of course, run along.

00:28:40.180 --> 00:28:44.040
I'm sorry I couldn't get rid of that gentleman that came here with a bill from Putnam's.

00:28:44.240 --> 00:28:45.140
Don't worry about it.

00:28:45.160 --> 00:28:46.380
I sent him over to Mr. Lexton.

00:28:46.560 --> 00:28:47.520
He'll know how to deal with it.

00:28:47.890 --> 00:28:48.190
Good.

00:28:48.520 --> 00:28:50.940
And I hope he gives him a piece of his mind, too.

00:28:51.360 --> 00:28:51.620
Hello.

00:28:52.780 --> 00:28:53.380
Oh, Roger.

00:28:54.800 --> 00:28:56.240
Did you have a nice time on the yacht?

00:28:58.360 --> 00:28:59.960
Anything that Miles Rushworth does is...

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:09.890
news why haven't you telephoned me no i certainly don't think it's for the best is that the rushworth

00:29:09.890 --> 00:29:20.090
influence i'm sorry no no please don't hang up ivy i i must see you today if you won't come here

00:29:20.090 --> 00:29:25.820
then i'll go to you oh yes i would i'll expect you in an hour goodbye

00:29:42.600 --> 00:29:43.540
Why are you looking like that?

00:29:44.100 --> 00:29:45.040
Got the sack or something?

00:29:45.300 --> 00:29:45.800
Not yet.

00:29:46.890 --> 00:29:47.630
Your party over?

00:29:48.770 --> 00:29:49.130
Apparently.

00:29:52.260 --> 00:29:54.440
Did you have to send that bill collector across to the office?

00:29:55.140 --> 00:29:56.720
Oh, you mean that man from Putnam's?

00:29:56.930 --> 00:29:59.410
Here I am, trying to establish myself in a decent job.

00:30:00.160 --> 00:30:03.220
What sort of impression do you think it makes to have tradesmen dunning me on the office steps?

00:30:03.520 --> 00:30:05.400
Darling, you look so funny when you're angry.

00:30:05.520 --> 00:30:06.500
Well, I'm not feeling funny.

00:30:06.720 --> 00:30:08.040
Well, Angel, what else could I do?

00:30:08.180 --> 00:30:10.840
Putnam said they wouldn't leave another thing unless they had something on account.

00:30:10.940 --> 00:30:13.000
Well, perhaps if you'd knock off one or two of your bridge parties.

00:30:13.630 --> 00:30:15.570
And eat the life of a recluse. Is that what you want?

00:30:15.670 --> 00:30:16.830
Yes, we've got a pleasant flat.

00:30:16.990 --> 00:30:17.630
Kensington Gardens to walk in.

00:30:17.630 --> 00:30:19.310
And Peter Pan statue to talk to.

00:30:19.370 --> 00:30:20.770
You'd only make an effort to be reasonable.

00:30:21.140 --> 00:30:22.440
Oh, it's all my fault, I suppose.

00:30:22.780 --> 00:30:26.560
I'm trying to get on my feet again, and here we are floundering into another ocean of bills.

00:30:26.960 --> 00:30:28.300
You used to want me to spend money.

00:30:28.400 --> 00:30:29.980
You used to be proud of my pretty dresses, and you...

00:30:30.030 --> 00:30:30.770
We've got neighbors.

00:30:31.770 --> 00:30:32.970
Well, you started the argument.

00:30:33.350 --> 00:30:34.270
I'm not even arguing.

00:30:34.430 --> 00:30:37.270
I'm merely trying to tell you that I haven't got Rushworth's millions.

00:30:37.730 --> 00:30:38.510
That's very true.

00:30:39.200 --> 00:30:40.580
I'm earning a thousand pounds a year.

00:30:40.660 --> 00:30:42.620
You can spend every penny of it in any way you please.

00:30:43.110 --> 00:30:45.130
If you spend more than I'm earning, we're back where we started.

00:30:47.490 --> 00:30:50.420
Dear Jarvis, you're absolutely right.

00:30:51.140 --> 00:30:51.300
Huh?

00:30:52.010 --> 00:30:53.670
I do make a mess of things, don't I?

00:30:54.900 --> 00:30:56.540
Managing everything so badly.

00:30:56.900 --> 00:30:58.180
Oh, I wouldn't say that.

00:30:58.300 --> 00:30:59.120
No, but it's true.

00:31:00.280 --> 00:31:03.440
Troubles and extravagances and debtors.

00:31:04.220 --> 00:31:07.390
Darling, why don't you do the same thing and get a divorce?

00:31:08.330 --> 00:31:10.070
I said I'll never divorce you in a million years.

00:31:10.330 --> 00:31:11.710
But think how much better off you'll be.

00:31:12.200 --> 00:31:14.240
I'd like you to follow me.

00:31:14.780 --> 00:31:15.820
You stir it up.

00:31:18.180 --> 00:31:22.490
Besides, how long do you think I'd keep this job without you as my sponsor?

00:31:22.670 --> 00:31:25.870
If we do go on, it'll be nothing but years of petty wrangling.

00:31:26.210 --> 00:31:27.590
We'll survive the wrangling?

00:31:28.110 --> 00:31:29.490
But we'll live those years out together.

00:31:30.890 --> 00:31:35.580
No, no, don't touch me. It only makes me feel worse.

00:31:37.640 --> 00:31:40.150
That's right. You have a good cry.

00:31:40.330 --> 00:31:44.150
I'll have a good walk and vent the rest of my spleen in that Peter Pan statue you talked about.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:09.160
Nothing wrong, Mr. Roger?

00:32:09.380 --> 00:32:09.940
No, nothing.

00:32:14.430 --> 00:32:15.310
I shan't want any tea.

00:32:16.430 --> 00:32:18.970
Oh, I wish.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:30.020
Thank you.

00:33:02.110 --> 00:33:02.630
Mr. Roger.

00:33:04.800 --> 00:33:05.440
Why, mother.

00:33:05.980 --> 00:33:07.660
Oh, my dear boy, don't look so bewildered.

00:33:07.780 --> 00:33:08.760
It's only the old lady.

00:33:09.080 --> 00:33:11.360
You didn't think I'd forget your birthday, did you?

00:33:11.520 --> 00:33:12.480
Oh, I forgot me myself.

00:33:13.030 --> 00:33:13.670
That's a cake.

00:33:13.790 --> 00:33:16.010
And I might be persuaded to stay and have dinner with you later.

00:33:16.420 --> 00:33:18.500
In the meantime, if Martha would get me some tea.

00:33:18.640 --> 00:33:19.720
You should be sure, Mom, and muffins.

00:33:19.860 --> 00:33:21.400
I know how partially you bought out of muffins.

00:33:21.400 --> 00:33:22.260
I'm sorry, Martha, no.

00:33:22.640 --> 00:33:24.000
Huh? No muffins?

00:33:24.140 --> 00:33:24.980
No tea, I'm afraid.

00:33:25.100 --> 00:33:25.860
Oh, what nonsense.

00:33:26.020 --> 00:33:26.960
Why, we've got oceans of tea.

00:33:26.980 --> 00:33:27.800
I don't mean that.

00:33:28.060 --> 00:33:29.200
Why, Roger, what is it?

00:33:29.570 --> 00:33:29.970
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:32.740
Sorry, Mother, but something urgent's come up.

00:33:32.990 --> 00:33:34.070
Are you throwing me out?

00:33:34.250 --> 00:33:35.950
No, not really, but it's...

00:33:36.170 --> 00:33:37.610
Well, you know how it is for a doctor.

00:33:37.810 --> 00:33:38.010
It's...

00:33:38.010 --> 00:33:39.610
It's a brainstorm by the look of you.

00:33:39.830 --> 00:33:42.990
I think you'd better come down and clear your head with the breath of our country air.

00:33:43.330 --> 00:33:44.410
I'll come down this weekend.

00:33:44.690 --> 00:33:48.490
Oh, well, in that case, I suppose I've got to forgive you for flinging your poor old mother out into the street.

00:33:49.610 --> 00:33:50.990
I'll make up for it this weekend.

00:33:51.950 --> 00:33:52.590
Just be patient.

00:33:53.150 --> 00:33:54.670
I'm not sure that patience is a virtue.

00:33:55.070 --> 00:33:56.690
However, you're much too big for a spanking.

00:33:57.120 --> 00:33:57.920
Goodbye, my boy.

00:33:58.020 --> 00:33:58.520
Goodbye, Mother.

00:33:59.110 --> 00:33:59.690
Goodbye, Martha.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:01.000
Take care of him.

00:34:01.160 --> 00:34:01.960
Yes, ma'am, I will.

00:34:02.980 --> 00:34:13.730
It's a funny way to behave, if I may say so.

00:34:13.810 --> 00:34:14.470
You may not say so.

00:34:14.610 --> 00:34:17.540
As you wish, off your feet for weeks and off your head today,

00:34:18.140 --> 00:34:20.100
as if my romantic wasn't enough to contend with it,

00:34:20.200 --> 00:34:22.700
having you carrying on like this, like a child of two years old.

00:34:38.830 --> 00:34:44.160
Darling, I don't suppose I should have said what I did on the telephone, but I can't say I'm sorry I brought you here.

00:34:44.340 --> 00:34:45.700
You must say you didn't give me much choice.

00:34:45.920 --> 00:34:47.140
You didn't give me much choice either.

00:34:48.310 --> 00:34:50.730
Terribly hurt when I found out you'd gone on the yacht with Rushworth.

00:34:51.200 --> 00:34:52.020
Jarvis was with me.

00:34:52.320 --> 00:34:53.480
Jarvis's presence is no assurance.

00:34:53.700 --> 00:34:54.380
Don't be upset.

00:34:54.700 --> 00:34:56.920
You think every man in London is in love with me.

00:34:57.100 --> 00:34:59.890
No man could be near you, touch you, or speak to you without foaming you.

00:35:01.180 --> 00:35:04.020
Oh, Roger, sometimes you say the silliest, nicest things.

00:35:04.360 --> 00:35:05.900
But if it would make you feel any better,

00:35:06.360 --> 00:35:08.960
Mr. Rashford's gone off to South Africa, perhaps for months.

00:35:10.140 --> 00:35:12.120
You know, you shouldn't have telephoned me this afternoon.

00:35:12.600 --> 00:35:16.240
Darling, I can't explain what happens to me when I don't see you or hear from you.

00:35:16.600 --> 00:35:19.860
Well, I've even thought of going to Jarvis and explaining everything to him, begging him to give you up.

00:35:20.340 --> 00:35:22.440
I've never made you dream of such a thing as going to Jarvis.

00:35:22.720 --> 00:35:25.680
You know he's refused time and time again to agree to a divorce.

00:35:25.780 --> 00:35:27.060
There's some consolation in that.

00:35:27.410 --> 00:35:29.630
If I can't make you my wife, neither can any other man.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:37.660
long as Jarvis lives. No, no. I'm sorry I'm at the end of my death. I know I am. What

00:35:37.660 --> 00:35:43.540
have I got to look forward to? Always party, always bills, always Jarvis. I can't go on

00:35:43.540 --> 00:35:52.620
like this. Roger, come pick your mother. I'm busy, Martha. Let me eat, please. Roger, please

00:35:52.620 --> 00:35:59.980
that's Roger. It's little Peter who liked you so much.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:01.240
She's beating something off them.

00:36:01.480 --> 00:36:01.980
I'll get you back.

00:36:01.980 --> 00:36:02.720
No, no, I'll get it.

00:36:02.800 --> 00:36:03.600
You get the interceptor.

00:36:03.640 --> 00:36:04.160
Yes, Miss Roger.

00:36:04.440 --> 00:36:05.360
I'll go try and...

00:36:05.360 --> 00:36:06.380
Where is Miss Roger?

00:36:06.580 --> 00:36:07.480
No, no, not that one.

00:36:07.680 --> 00:36:09.100
It's on the second shelf, behind those bottles.

00:36:12.610 --> 00:36:13.250
Here you are, sir.

00:36:13.880 --> 00:36:14.720
Tell him I'll be there in a moment.

00:36:14.840 --> 00:36:15.260
Yes, sir.

00:36:15.560 --> 00:36:22.020
You mustn't.

00:36:22.080 --> 00:36:22.360
Not yet.

00:36:22.940 --> 00:36:23.860
I'll only be ten minutes.

00:36:24.360 --> 00:36:25.540
Then we must talk things out.

00:36:25.720 --> 00:36:26.300
We've got to.

00:36:26.780 --> 00:36:28.400
There's a point at which one must make a decision.

00:36:29.140 --> 00:36:29.340
Wait.

00:36:30.410 --> 00:36:31.730
And wipe away those tears, darling.

00:38:05.880 --> 00:38:07.600
Sorry, Mom, I didn't know as no one was here.

00:38:08.660 --> 00:38:10.020
I just came to put the jars back.

00:39:03.900 --> 00:39:04.880
Hello there, my darling.

00:39:05.770 --> 00:39:06.590
Well, don't get up, dear.

00:39:07.720 --> 00:39:08.800
Thanks for calling me dear.

00:39:09.990 --> 00:39:11.290
More than I deserve, really.

00:39:12.810 --> 00:39:14.390
I began to feel you left me for good.

00:39:16.680 --> 00:39:19.180
Oh, I found the debris on the carpet before Emily did.

00:39:19.400 --> 00:39:21.310
Put it in the side drawer.

00:39:22.580 --> 00:39:23.780
I'm sorry I broke your...

00:39:24.580 --> 00:39:26.360
Don't you go apologizing to me.

00:39:28.700 --> 00:39:29.980
Wouldn't get me another brandy and soda.

00:39:30.090 --> 00:39:30.590
Would you, darling?

00:40:31.790 --> 00:40:35.510
You're an angel. Don't ever let's quarrel a game.

00:40:38.020 --> 00:40:49.410
Well, Min Jin seems a little bitter.

00:41:01.020 --> 00:41:02.000
It's Lex, yes?

00:41:02.960 --> 00:41:06.620
I'm sorry to disturb him, but Mr. Lexter was ill in the night.

00:41:07.240 --> 00:41:09.600
I wanted to send for a doctor, but he wouldn't let me.

00:41:10.790 --> 00:41:11.430
I'll be right there.

00:41:52.200 --> 00:41:53.520
What is it? Something you've eaten?

00:41:54.560 --> 00:41:55.620
I've swallowed a salamide.

00:41:57.390 --> 00:41:57.650
Yes.

00:42:00.030 --> 00:42:07.840
throat's burning. The great coat's just too many brandies and sodas. Emily shouldn't have bothered

00:42:07.840 --> 00:42:14.160
you. Emily should have bothered me much sooner. Right. The heavy day of the office coming. No,

00:42:14.280 --> 00:42:18.360
Jarvis, you mustn't go to the office. I tell you what, Ivy, you just slipped me a hair of the dog.

00:42:19.080 --> 00:42:28.830
Brandy and soda'd make me feel right as rain. Don't look so shocked. A little one and not too much soda.

00:42:30.350 --> 00:42:32.070
Jarvis, I do hate to see you in pain.

00:42:32.270 --> 00:42:34.160
Pain should be quick.

00:42:35.320 --> 00:42:36.380
Something that's over quickly.

00:42:36.980 --> 00:42:37.800
I'll second that.

00:42:39.110 --> 00:42:40.370
I'll get you the brandy and soda.

00:43:43.180 --> 00:43:44.140
He's worse again.

00:43:44.550 --> 00:43:45.190
Who's with him?

